00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.150
You went to school like that?

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.770
Yup. Glistening lips and eyes like a panda.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:30.900
A panda?

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.350
She's here.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.480
She is?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.600
But...

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.730
...she's skipping.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.850
What's up?

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.350
I wonder.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:42.770
Now she's lashing out.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:43.810
Huh?

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.020
Why's she doing that?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.230
I don't know. Maybe something happened.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.730
I've had a nightmare like this.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.690
It ended horribly.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.400
Let's just watch for a bit.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.600
Congratulations. I see you managed to escape.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.350
Yeah, but what's with those Haters?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:17.310
Who asked them to treat us like heroes?
We're not doing this for fun.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.480
Regrettably, they can't be reasoned with.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.650
Those who stand out pay for it,
in any time and in any world.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.600
Didn't you say you "had a solution in mind"?

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.730
Yes. Look, here it is now.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.400
Thanks.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.850
That case contains things that will support you.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:41.940
Basically, it's what you call a "power up."

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.150
Like what?

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.020
Beats me.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.850
I doubt we'll get to use it all the time.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.060
If you've got something
that handy, say so sooner!

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.400
These are extremely valuable.
We couldn't have you losing them.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.440
That means, "Don't get used to it, idiots."

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.100
They're super cute!

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:14.230
You can have them free of charge.
One each, of course.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.440
Pendants?

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.230
Pomanders, right?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.150
Wow.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.270
So, how do we use them?

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.980
First, you hatch them in this world.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.400
Hatch them?

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.350
It's not so difficult.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:34.520
They respond to body heat, so clasp them
in both hands and gently rub them.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.480
Oh, but don't do it here.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.730
Go home and open them when you're alone.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.150
Why?

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.150
They require imprinting.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.600
They see whoever meets
their gaze first as their parent.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.350
Chant " <i>veni</i> " to call them from their eggs.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.020
" <i>Redi</i> " to return them.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.520
Latin?

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.190
I hope my baby's a hottie.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.020
Hey, what types do you think are in them?

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.980
We haven't imprinted yet,
so we can trade, right?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.150
Wanna swap with me, Neiru?

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.230
No.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.020
I hope you get the ugliest helper.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.150
Ai...

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.190
...is something wrong?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.270
You seem different.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.100
It's a long story.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.520
I'm leaving now, Ma'am.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.770
Fine.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:49.850
<i>Veni</i> .

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.690
A snake.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.690
Hello?

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.400
I'm not sure how to react.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.190
Again?

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:18.440
Don't worry. We've got backup this time.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.440
<i>Veni</i> .

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.020
He ate it!

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.310
Haters are their favorite food.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.940
Envy and spite are their bread and butter.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.190
Okay, I'm counting on you!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.270
That should solve our Hater problem.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.560
What's wrong?

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:55.400
Yae, why did you kill yourself?

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.520
I can see.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.400
See what?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:04.150
Dead people, strong grudges...

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:06.270
Like The Sixth Sense?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.310
See?! No one will believe me.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:14.230
There are unbelievably scary things
that only I can see.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:18.190
Sorry. I don't understand.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.400
It's fine.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.770
My friends left because it creeped them out.

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.900
My parents and teachers wouldn't believe me.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:29.190
In fact, they thought I was crazy
and put me in a hospital.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.480
But what really scared me was what came next.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.650
What?

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:38.520
That hospital was overflowing
with lots of people's resentment.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.480
It was way worse than ghosts.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:44.480
Those people's voices and their terrifying faces

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.230
poured into my head day in and day out!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.230
Calm down!

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:52.560
Listen, a boss is coming. I'll get ready for it.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.940
It's already here!

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:54.940
Huh?

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.400
Good evening, Ohto.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.810
G-Good evening.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.900
It's dinner time, so dry your hair quickly.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.730
Oh, I'll help you.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.150
Oh, no, I'm fine.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:29.150
Please take a seat.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:30.150
Huh?

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:31.520
He's staying...?

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:37.920
Here.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.520
Thank you very much.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:43.270
Thanks for dinner.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.940
Ai, wait a moment.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.560
Ai.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.900
We have something to tell you.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.770
If it's school, I need a little more--

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.770
It's not school. Just sit down.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.850
Listen calmly, okay?

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:16.190
We've been thinking that
we'd like to start dating.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:29.020
Of course, we're not going to do
anything if you're not okay with it.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.480
My uncle and Ai's mom?

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:50.310
That means we might end up being family!

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.600
What are you excited for?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.060
Well, I mean...

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.190
Right, Ai?

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:58.900
Does she look happy to you?

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:01.900
Are you against it?

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:05.350
I told them to do whatever.
It's none of my business.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.900
Well, you fought as hard as you could.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:12.150
And that I wouldn't take care of them
or live with them in the future.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:15.730
I said I'd put them in a home
and only visit sometimes.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.480
Nice. You really let 'em have it.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.900
Why? Do you feel bad for your real dad?

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.020
No. They're already divorced,

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:27.020
and Dad might have someone new himself.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.650
Then, there's no problem.

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:31.480
There is.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:34.150
Don't you listen to people, Momoe?

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:39.190
You mean that my uncle might have
been involved in Koito's suicide?

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.650
I told you, there's no way.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.440
And what if there was?

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.560
Mr. Sawaki's younger than Ai's mom.

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.270
He'd be her younger live-in boyfriend.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.440
So?

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.520
"So"?

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:54.020
Live-in boyfriends are always
abusing their girlfriends' kids.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:58.350
Violently if it's a son,
sexually if it’s a daughter.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.400
I'm sorry,

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:03.560
but don't lump my uncle in
with the men your mom's dated.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:05.150
What'd you say?!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.650
You mean it's possible that
Mr. Sawaki likes young girls like us,

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:12.350
meaning that Ai's mom is a decoy
and he's really after Ai?

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:17.810
No way. Besides, he knows that Ai's my friend.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.270
I don't think it's like that.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:26.310
I just... don't like not knowing about Koito.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:31.600
If they marry, you'll have to
cover for him to protect your mom.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:34.060
Unbelievable. I've heard enough.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.020
I'm sorry, Momo. That's not what I...

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.850
What on Earth are they talking about?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.060
No clue.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:45.770
Not what clothes would go with
those necklaces, that's for sure.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:50.810
Sometimes, family matters take
precedence over life-or-death battles.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:56.520
I guess we'll never know the truth
unless we bring Koito back and ask her.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:59.100
Occam's razor.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:02.230
There might be a factor complicating matters.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:03.060
Huh?

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:07.310
What? There's <i>more</i> ?!

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.270
Ai likes Mr. Sawaki, too.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.600
Oh! Yeah!

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:14.690
"The simplest theory is the best."

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.190
What do you mean, Neiru?!

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:18.770
You're wrong! I don't...

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:19.810
Emotional!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.060
Complicated and emotional!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.400
I don't! That's totally impossible!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:33.020
Stop!

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.770
Stay away!

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:38.690
I didn't ask to be able to see you.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:41.810
I'm not your friend or anything like that!

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.850
No!

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.060
No...

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.400
Stop it!

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.100
It's here?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.560
But I can't...

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:13.600
Please,

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.690
don't kill that girl!

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:20.350
Prayer beads?

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:27.940
You mean that my uncle might have
been involved in Koito's suicide?

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:35.310
We've been thinking that
we'd like to start dating.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.940
There might be a factor complicating matters.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.810
There's no reason to have a complex.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:53.440
Your eyes are charming.

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:58.150
Ai likes Mr. Sawaki, too.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:02.520
No.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.560
I don't.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.770
No!

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:17.770
I don't.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.060
Don't tell me...

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:24.480
I'm telling you, I don't!

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:43.150
Now I'm really mad!

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.060
You can see me, Miss?

00:17:57.060 --> 00:18:01.310
Yeah. But I can't be your friend.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.980
I bet it was tough,

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.020
dealing with these monsters all on your own.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.350
You believe me?

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.900
Of course.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:29.190
Your name is Leon.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:30.560
Not very creative.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.650
<i>Veni</i> .

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.060
<i>Redi</i> .

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:43.650
<i>Veni</i> .

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:51.810
Ai, Mr. Sawaki is leaving.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.600
Don't mind me.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:56.190
See you next week, Ohto.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:04.350
"It might rain, so take in the laundry, okay?
There's melon in the fridge."

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.940
I'm home.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.730
In the bath, Ai?

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.310
Welcome back.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.600
Oh, don't leave your dirty clothes here.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:22.350
What do I always tell you?

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:25.730
Turn the pockets inside-out for washing.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.690
I'll leave what was in your pockets here.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.060
Hey!

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:38.650
Ai?!

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:39.440
You'll catch cold!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.480
I'm fine!

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.650
Where are you going dressed like that?

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.770
School!

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:46.850
Huh?!

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.560
Bye-bye, Mr. S.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:26.810
Goodbye.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:30.980
Mr. Sawaki.

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.060
Ohto?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.190
What's wrong?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.350
Ohto.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:01.560
The sky is clear and beautiful.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:04.230
It was a passing shower.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.230
I...!

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.650
I'm...

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.810
...going to go to school!

00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:01.940
Next time

00:22:58.310 --> 00:22:59.480
To be continued.
